### Structured Outputs (Tool Use Method)

```python
# Define structured response tool
json_tool = {
    "name": "structured_response",
    "description": "Provide structured analysis",
    "input_schema": {
        "type": "object",
        "properties": {
            "analysis": {"type": "string"},
            "recommendations": {"type": "array", "items": {"type": "string"}},
            "confidence": {"type": "number", "minimum": 0, "maximum": 1}
        },
        "required": ["analysis", "recommendations", "confidence"]
    }
}

response = requests.post(
    "https://api.anthropic.com/v1/messages",
    headers={
        "x-api-key": ANTHROPIC_API_KEY,
        "anthropic-version": "2023-06-01"
    },
    json={
        "model": "claude-3-5-sonnet-20241022",
        "max_tokens": 1024,
        "tools": [json_tool],
        "tool_choice": {"type": "tool", "name": "structured_response"},
        "messages": [
            {"role": "user", "content": "Analyze this business scenario"}
        ]
    }
)
```

### Refusal Handling

```python
def handle_anthropic_response(response):
    """Handle Anthropic API responses with refusal detection."""
    content = response.json()["content"][0]["text"]
    
    # Check for common refusal patterns
    refusal_indicators = [
        "I can't assist with",
        "I'm not able to",
        "I don't feel comfortable",
        "That request could be harmful"
    ]
    
    is_refusal = any(indicator in content for indicator in refusal_indicators)
    
    if is_refusal:
        return {"type": "refusal", "message": content}
    else:
        return {"type": "success", "content": content}
```

